  "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"minus 15 x plus 25 y equals 65\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t<mn>15</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>25</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>65</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">One of the two equations in a system of linear equations is given. The system has infinitely many solutions. Which of the following could be the second equation in the system?</p>",
